[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is the following expected?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Insert</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FinCases</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: Tactic `cases` failed with a nested error:</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">Dependent elimination failed: Failed to solve equation</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Decidable.rec (fun h =&gt; (fun x =&gt; [a, b]) h) (fun h =&gt; (fun x =&gt; [b]) h) (instDecidableEqBool ([b].contains a) true) =</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">    x :: as✝</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">at case `List.Mem.head`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fin_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>According to the doc of <code>fin_cases</code> (\"<code>fin_cases h</code> performs case analysis on a hypothesis of the form <code>h : A</code>, where <code>[Fintype A]</code> is available, or <code>h : a ∈ A</code>, where <code>A : Finset X</code>, <code>A : Multiset X</code> or <code>A : List X</code>.\"), this should work</p>",
        "id": 601018181,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780861157
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>based on having read the implementation of <code>fin_cases</code>, I can see why this would happen</p>",
        "id": 601018320,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780861228
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>the problem is that <code>{a, b}</code> is actually something like <code>if h : a = b then {b} else cons a {b} ⋯</code>, so we don't know if we have one case or two cases</p>",
        "id": 601018455,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780861356
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It looks like the situation in my example is not covered by the tests in <code>MathlibTest.Tactic.FinCases</code>.</p>",
        "id": 601018554,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780861445
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this example would not be doable without basically rewriting the whole thing from scratch</p>",
        "id": 601018598,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780861483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/fin_cases.20error.20on.20a.20Finset/near/601018455\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the problem is that <code>{a, b}</code> is actually something like <code>if h : a = b then {b} else cons a {b} ⋯</code>, so we don't know if we have one case or two cases</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>We should just generate two cases here. This cannot be wrong.</p>",
        "id": 601018601,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780861485
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is a work-around:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Insert</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FinCases</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">replace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fin_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tauto</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Could this be incorporated as a kind of preprocessing step?</p>",
        "id": 601018760,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780861627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>how would this work? currently <code>fin_cases</code> only handles <code>h : a ∈ A</code> when <code>A</code> reduces to applications of the constructors</p>",
        "id": 601018954,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780861803
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Shouldn't it rather be something like <code>Finset.insert a (FInset.insert b Finset.empty)</code>, which would make it easy to generate the relevant cases from it?</p>",
        "id": 601019379,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780862193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>{a, b}</code> means <code>insert a (singleton b)</code></p>",
        "id": 601019449,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780862261
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>also, <code>fin_cases</code> works on stuff that isn't of that form</p>",
        "id": 601019466,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780862280
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The question is why it doesn't work on <code>insert a (singleton b)</code>. It could consider <code>insert</code> (and <code>singleton</code>) as a constructor, I assume?</p>",
        "id": 601019565,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780862361
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>for example, here it's casing on <code>x ∈ Finset.univ</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ZMod</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">13</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fin_cases</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;;&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 601019571,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780862371
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"479359\">Michael Stoll</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/fin_cases.20error.20on.20a.20Finset/near/601019565\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The question is why it doesn't work on <code>insert a (singleton b)</code>. It could consider <code>insert</code> (and <code>singleton</code>) as a constructor, I assume?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The constructor for <code>Finset</code> is <code>Finset.mk</code>, and the constructor for <code>Multiset</code> is <code>Multiset.ofList</code>, and the constructors for <code>List</code> are <code>List.nil</code> and <code>List.cons</code></p>",
        "id": 601019620,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780862412
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>so no, <code>insert</code> is not a constructor, though <code>singleton</code> does reduce to an application of <code>Finset.mk</code></p>",
        "id": 601019920,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780862679
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess what I mean is that the <code>unfoldCases</code> procedure could be slightly more clever and check for, e.g., <code>x ∈ insert a s</code>, and then split into <code>x = a</code> and <code>x ∈ s</code>.</p>",
        "id": 601019956,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780862707
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(In any case, a more informative error message would be nice.)</p>",
        "id": 601019998,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1780862746
    }
]